# Proxy backend endpoints same-origin for arten-fördern.ch (Netlify):
# auth needs same-origin because session cookies can never cross the
# .ch/.app TLD boundary (SameSite); PostgREST's CORS only allows .app.
# The .app frontend keeps calling the API subdomains directly.
#
# The SPA's login page lives at EXACTLY /auth — without the explicit rule
# below, the /auth/* proxy also matches the bare path (the splat matches
# empty) and Netlify forwards it to the auth server, which 404s
# ("Cannot GET /auth/"). Everything else under /auth/* (API calls, the
# OAuth callback) belongs to the auth server.
# NB: a rule for /auth/ (trailing slash) is futile — netlify matches it to
# the /auth/* proxy with an empty splat no matter what comes first; nothing
# generates /auth/ links, so it stays a 404.
/auth     /index.html  200
/auth/*  https://auth.xn--arten-frdern-bjb.app/auth/:splat  200
/api/*   https://api.xn--arten-frdern-bjb.app/:splat        200

/*    /index.html   200
